// A backfill can be worked out from each stored row's own fields: here
// the crates a delivery used, from its boxes, through the same library
// function `record_delivery` uses. `Delivery.boxes` means each row's
// stored value. The rows are filled in batches, each its own
// transaction, so a long table is never locked for the whole backfill;
// then the field is made required.

/// Counts the crates every delivery already made used.
migration {
    Delivery.crates_used: {
        backfill: crates.for_boxes(Delivery.boxes)
    }
}
